 ("canaanite","anat","Anat","the warrior goddess of the Baal Cycle wading in blood, the killer of Mot, the Aqhat epic and the bow, Anat in Egypt (Ramesses II's daughter's name), Anat-Yahu at Elephantine, the Anat-Bethel of the Aramaic texts"),
 ("canaanite","astarte","Astarte","Athtart of Ugarit, the Ashtoreth of the Bible (Solomon's Sidonian goddess), the Astarte of Sidon and Tyre and the Phoenician colonies, the Pyrgi tablets with Uni, the Astarte of Egypt as warrior, the Aphrodite identification at Cyprus, the Ishtar cognate"),
 ("canaanite","yam","Yam","the sea god defeated by Baal with Kothar's two clubs (KTU 1.2), Judge River, the Yam of the Bible's chaos combat (Psalm 74, Isaiah 51), the Yam-Tiamat and Yam-Leviathan relations"),
 ("canaanite","mot","Mot","Death who swallows Baal, Anat's threshing and grinding of him, the seven-year cycle and the return (KTU 1.5-6), the Mot of the Bible's personified death (Isaiah 25:8, Hosea 13:14), the Muth of Philo of Byblos"),
 ("canaanite","dagon","Dagon","Dagan of Ebla, Mari and Tuttul, the father of Baal at Ugarit, the Philistine Dagon of Ashdod and the fallen idol (1 Samuel 5), the fish-god misreading (Jerome onward) and its Lovecraftian afterlife, the Dagan of the Assyrian kings"),
 ("canaanite","melqart","Melqart","the king of the city of Tyre, the awakening (egersis) festival and the Greek Heracles identification, the temple at Tyre (Herodotus II.44, the two pillars), the Melqart of Gadir and the Pillars of Hercules, the Bar-Hadad stela, the Carthaginian Melqart and Hannibal's oath, Bonnet's Melqart"),
 ("canaanite","eshmun","Eshmun","the healing god of Sidon, the temple at Bostan esh-Sheikh and the child statues, the Asclepius identification, the Eshmun of Carthage's Byrsa temple destroyed in 146, the Eshmunazar sarcophagus"),
 ("canaanite","resheph","Resheph","the plague and war god with the gazelle head, the Rashap of Ebla and Ugarit, the Resheph of Egypt's New Kingdom stelae, the biblical reshef (Habakkuk 3:5), Apollo of the Cypriot bilinguals"),
 ("canaanite","shapash","Shapash","the sun goddess of Ugarit, the torch of the gods, the messenger of El who finds Baal's body, the Shapash of the ritual texts and the Rephaim"),
 ("canaanite","yarikh","Yarikh","the moon god of Ugarit, the Marriage of Nikkal and Yarikh, Jericho's name, the Yarikh of the Phoenician theophoric names"),
 ("canaanite","kothar_wa_khasis","Kothar-wa-Khasis","the craftsman god of Ugarit who made Baal's clubs and palace and Aqhat's bow, from Caphtor (Crete) and Memphis, the Chousor of Philo of Byblos, the Ptah and Hephaestus comparisons"),
 ("canaanite","baal_hammon","Baal Hammon","the chief god of Carthage, the tophet and the child sacrifice question (the stelae, the Diodorus and Plutarch accounts, the osteological debate: Schwartz versus Smith and Stager), Saturn Africanus, Tanit's partner, the Hammon etymology"),
 ("canaanite","adonis","Adonis","the Phoenician Adon at Byblos and the Adonis river running red, Lucian's De Dea Syria, the Greek Adonis of Sappho and Theocritus's Idyll 15, the Adonia festival and the gardens, Tammuz as source, the Frazer dying god and its critics"),
 ("canaanite","baalat_gebal","Baalat Gebal","the Lady of Byblos, Hathor-identified, the Yehawmilk stela, the Obelisk Temple and the Byblos-Egypt trade, the Baalat of the Wenamun report"),
 ("canaanite","chemosh","Chemosh","the god of Moab, the Mesha Stela's Chemosh who was angry with his land, Solomon's high place, the Kamish of Ebla, the herem to Chemosh"),
 ("canaanite","milcom","Milcom","the god of Ammon, the Amman citadel inscription, the Solomon high places, the Milcom-Molech confusion and the 'Malcam' readings, the Ammonite theophoric names"),
 ("canaanite","qadesh","Qadesh (Qetesh)","the Holy One, the naked goddess on the lion of the Egyptian stelae flanked by Min and Resheph (the Qadesh stela, British Museum), the Syrian goddess imported, the Athirat epithet question"),
 ("canaanite","horon","Horon","the underworld and snake-charm god of Ugarit (the serpent incantation KTU 1.100), the Beth-Horon place-names, the Egyptian Hauron at Giza as the Sphinx (the Ramesside identification)"),
 ("canaanite","attar","Attar","the Venus god who tried Baal's throne and found his feet did not reach the footstool (KTU 1.6), the South Arabian Athtar and the Astarte masculine counterpart, the morning star"),
 ("canaanite","lotan","Lotan (Leviathan's source)","the seven-headed sea serpent defeated by Baal and Anat (KTU 1.3, 1.5), the Leviathan of Isaiah 27 and Psalm 74 as its heir (own file in abrahamic/), the Litan of the Ugaritic incantations"),
 ("canaanite","shahar_and_shalim","Shahar and Shalim","Dawn and Dusk, the Gracious Gods born of El and two women (KTU 1.23), the Jerusalem name and the Shalem of the Bible, the Lucifer-Shahar connection in Isaiah 14 (Helel ben Shahar)"),
 ("canaanite","nikkal","Nikkal","the orchard goddess bride of Yarikh, the Nikkal hymn as the oldest notated music (the Hurrian hymn h.6 and the reconstructions), Ningal as source"),
 ("canaanite","kotharat","The Kotharat","the birth goddesses, the swallows of Aqhat's conception (KTU 1.17), the seven wise women of the marriage texts"),
 ("canaanite","rephaim","The Rephaim","the deified dead kings of Ugarit (the Rephaim texts, KTU 1.20-22), the shades of the biblical Sheol, the giants of Bashan and Og, the Rapiuma feast, the Hebrew rephaim double meaning"),
 # ---------------- ANDEAN ----------------
 ("andean","viracocha","Viracocha","the creator of Tiwanaku and Lake Titicaca, the making of the sun and the people from stones, the wanderer who walked away over the sea, Betanzos, Molina, Sarmiento, the Coricancha's Viracocha and the Cusco temple of Kiswarkancha, the Spanish 'white god' reading and its critics, the Wiracocha of the Spaniards' name"),
 ("andean","mama_quilla","Mama Quilla","Mother Moon, wife of Inti, the silver room of the Coricancha, the eclipses as attacks by a puma, the moon's calendar and the women's cult, the Coya's patroness, the Quilla of the Huarochirí"),
 ("andean","illapa","Illapa","thunder and lightning with the sling and club, the Milky Way's water, Inti's third companion in the Coricancha, Santiago as his successor (Santiago Illapa of the Andes), the illapa mummies' name, the Apu Illapa of Huarochirí"),
 ("andean","mama_cocha","Mama Cocha","Mother Sea and lake, the coastal cult, the mother of Inti and Mama Quilla in some accounts, the fish and the whales, the Titicaca as Mama Cocha"),
 ("andean","supay","Supay","the lord of the underworld (ukhu pacha) turned Devil by the missionaries, the Supay of the Diablada of Oruro and the Tío of the Potosí mines, the Supay of the Quechua dictionaries (Holguín), the ambivalence of the original"),
 ("andean","pachacamac","Pachacamac","the earth-maker of the coast, the oracle and pilgrimage at the temple south of Lima, the Hernando Pizarro looting (1533), the Pachacamac idol found in 1938, the Con and Pachacamac myth (Calancha, the Huarochirí Manuscript), the Ychsma lords, the Inca's coexistence"),
 ("andean","manco_capac","Manco Capac","the founder from Titicaca (or Pacaritambo) with the golden staff that sank at Cusco, the son of the Sun, the Ayar brothers' cave, Garcilaso's version against Sarmiento's, the Manco Capac of the Inca dynastic paintings and the Peruvian nation"),
 ("andean","mama_ocllo","Mama Ocllo","the sister-wife of Manco Capac who taught the women weaving, Titicaca's daughter of the Sun, the Coya line, Guaman Poma's portrait, the Mama Ocllo of the Peruvian schoolbooks"),
 ("andean","ayar_brothers","The Ayar Brothers","the four brothers and four sisters from Pacaritambo's caves (Ayar Cachi walled in the cave, Ayar Uchu turned to stone at Huanacauri, Ayar Auca the stone of Cusco), Sarmiento and Betanzos, the huaca of Huanacauri, Urton's history of a myth"),
 ("andean","chasca","Chasca","Venus as the goddess of dawn and the flowers (Chaska Qoyllur), the page of the Sun, the young women's patroness, the Chasca of Guaman Poma"),
 ("andean","kon","Kon","the boneless wind god of the coast who made the first people and dried the land when insulted, displaced by Pachacamac (Gómara, Calancha), the Con of the Huarochirí's Coniraya"),
 ("andean","urcuchillay","Urcuchillay","the llama god of the herders, the dark-cloud constellation of the llama (Yacana) in the Milky Way, the Urcuchillay of Polo de Ondegardo, the llama sacrifices"),
 ("andean","apus","The Apus","the mountain lords as living gods: Ausangate, Salkantay, Illimani, the Apu of every community, the despacho offerings and the paqos, the Qoyllur Rit'i pilgrimage, the mountain sacrifices (Llullaillaco's children, Ampato's Juanita), the Apus in Argentine Salta and Jujuy"),
 ("andean","amaru","Amaru","the double-headed serpent of the waters and the underworld, the Amaru of Tiwanaku and Inca iconography, Tupac Amaru's name and the 1780 rebellion's appropriation, the Amaru of the Andean flood myths and the rainbow"),
 ("andean","ekeko","Ekeko","the pot-bellied god of abundance of the Alasitas fair (La Paz, January 24), the miniatures and the cigarette, the pre-Columbian Iqiqu of Tiwanaku, the 1781 siege legend, the returned stone Ekeko from Bern (2014)"),
 ("andean","coniraya_and_cavillace","Coniraya and Cavillace","the trickster Coniraya Viracocha who impregnated Cavillace with a fruit, the flight to the sea and the rocks of Pachacamac, the animals blessed and cursed on the road (the Huarochirí Manuscript chapter 2)"),
 ("andean","huallallo_carhuincho","Huallallo Carhuincho","the fire-god eater of children of the Huarochirí Manuscript, defeated by Pariacaca's five brothers' rain, exiled to the Antisuyu, the Yauyos-Huanca conflict behind the myth"),
 ("andean","pariacaca","Pariacaca","the five-fold mountain god born from five eggs (Huarochirí Manuscript), the flood against Huallallo, the Pariacaca snow-peak and pass on the Inca road, the Yauyos' ancestor, the modern pilgrimages"),
 ("andean","catequil","Catequil","the thunder oracle of Huamachuco destroyed by Atahualpa (the Augustinian relación), the twin brothers born of the sky, the oracle's stones and its huaca, the Catequil of the extirpators"),
 ("andean","mama_sara","Mama Sara","Mother Maize, the double ears kept as saramama, the corn dolls of the harvest, the Sara of the Coricancha's golden maize, the chicha and the Aymoray festival"),
 # ---------------- YORUBA ----------------
 ("yoruba","olodumare","Olodumare (Olorun)","the supreme god of the sky without cult or image, the names Olodumare and Olorun and the etymology debates, Idowu's monotheist reading and its critics (Peel, the missionary shaping of 'Olorun'), the Ifá verses on his relation to the orisha, the Cuban Olofi/Olodumare/Olorun triad"),
 ("yoruba","obatala","Obatala (Oxalá)","the creator of bodies and king of the white cloth, the drunk creation and the deformed as his children, the Ife kingship and the Oduduwa rivalry, the Igbo festival of Ife, the palm wine taboo, Obatalá in Cuba (Our Lady of Mercy) and Oxalá in Bahia (the Friday whites, Senhor do Bonfim, the Lavagem)"),
 ("yoruba","orunmila","Orunmila (Ifá)","the witness of destiny and lord of Ifá divination, the 256 Odu and the opele and ikin, Bascom's and Abimbola's corpora, the babalawo, the Ifá of Cuba (Orula) and the Ifá revival, the 2005 UNESCO listing of Ifá"),
 ("yoruba","eshu_elegua","Eshu / Elegua (Exu)","the trickster and messenger at the crossroads, the ashe carrier, the first fed, the missionaries' identification with the Devil (Crowther's Bible) and its consequences, Elegguá of Cuba with the child's face, Exu of Candomblé and the Umbanda Exus and Pomba Giras as a distinct development, Eshu in Ifá verses"),
 ("yoruba","ogun","Ogun (Ogum)","iron, war, the hunt and the road, the first to cut a path, the oath on iron in courts, the Ogun of drivers and surgeons, Ogun's rage and his withdrawal to Ire, Ogun in Cuba (St Peter) and Ogum in Brazil (St George in Rio, St Anthony in Bahia), Soyinka's Ogun, Barnes's Africa's Ogun"),
 ("yoruba","shango","Shango (Xangô, Changó)","the fourth Alaafin of Oyo made god of thunder, the hanging that did not happen (oba ko so), the double axe and the thunderstones, the bata drums, the Oyo empire's royal cult, the Cuban Changó (St Barbara) and the Bahian Xangô, the Shango of Trinidad, Rotimi's play"),
 ("yoruba","oya","Oya (Iansã)","the wind and the Niger, Shango's wife who tore the veil of the dead, the buffalo woman, the Egungun's mother, the market, Oya in Cuba (St Teresa, the cemetery gates) and Iansã in Brazil (St Barbara), the nine"),
 ("yoruba","oshun","Oshun (Oxum, Ochún)","the river of Osogbo, sweetness, fertility and brass, the only woman among the founding orisha in the Ifá verse, the Osun-Osogbo grove (Susanne Wenger, UNESCO 2005), Ochún of Cuba (La Caridad del Cobre, the national patroness) and Oxum of Brazil, the honey and the mirror"),
 ("yoruba","yemoja","Yemoja (Yemayá, Iemanjá)","the mother of fish and of the orisha, the Ogun river in Yorubaland and the sea in the Americas, Yemayá of Regla (Our Lady of Regla) and the Iemanjá of the February 2 festival at Rio Vermelho and New Year at Copacabana, the Argentine and Uruguayan beach cults (Montevideo's Playa Ramírez), the mermaid image and its Mami Wata and European sources"),
 ("yoruba","babalu_aye","Babalu-Aye (Shopona, Obaluaiê, Omolu)","the smallpox god whose name was not spoken, the Shopona cult's suppression by the British (1907) and the vaccination politics, the Dahomean Sakpata, Babalú-Ayé of Cuba (St Lazarus, the Rincón pilgrimage of December 17, Desi Arnaz's song) and Omolu/Obaluaiê of Bahia with the straw hood"),
 ("yoruba","osanyin","Osanyin (Ossaim)","the one-legged, one-eyed lord of leaves and medicine, the herbal knowledge of the onishegun, the bird staff, the Cuban Osain and the Brazilian Ossaim, the ewe (leaf) songs"),
 ("yoruba","oshosi","Oshosi (Oxóssi, Ochosi)","the hunter with the bow, the Ketu king, Ochosi of Cuba (the jail and the justice, St Norbert) and Oxóssi of Bahia as king of Ketu and patron of Candomblé's oldest houses, the Caboclo overlap in Umbanda"),
 ("yoruba","olokun","Olokun","the deep sea, male in Benin and female in some Yoruba cults, the Ife bronzes and the Olokun grove, the wealth of the deep, the Cuban Olokun of the Ifá priests (the masked dance, the chained deity) and the Brazilian near-absence"),
 ("yoruba","aganju","Aganju","the volcano and the wilderness, the Oyo king, the ferryman, Aganjú of Cuba (St Christopher, the Havana patron) and the Brazilian Aganju as an aspect of Xangô, the Shango-Aganju confusion"),
 ("yoruba","oba","Oba","Shango's first wife who cut off her ear on Oshun's advice, the river Oba, the jealousy myth and its versions, Obá in Cuba and Brazil with the covered ear, the wronged wife's cult"),
 ("yoruba","nana_buruku","Nana Buruku (Nanã)","the old mother of the swamp and the mud of creation, the Dahomean Nana Buluku who bore Mawu-Lisa, the ibiri, the taboo on iron and the quarrel with Ogun, Nanã of Bahia as the oldest orisha, the Cuban Naná Burukú"),
 ("yoruba","ibeji","The Ibeji","the twins as orisha, the ere ibeji figures and the twin cult (the world's highest twinning rate), the monkey and the twin mother's market begging, the Ibeyi of Cuba (Cosmas and Damian, the September 27 sweets) and the Erês of Brazil"),
 ("yoruba","oduduwa","Oduduwa","the founder of Ife and ancestor of the Yoruba kings, the descent by chain or the migration from the east (the Mecca legend of Johnson), Obatala's rival for the creation, the Ooni's cult, the Oduduwa of the Nigerian politics (the Egbe Omo Oduduwa, the 'Oduduwa Republic')"),
 ("yoruba","osumare","Osumare (Oxumaré)","the rainbow serpent, male and female by turns, the Dahomean Dan/Aido-Hwedo, the Brazilian Oxumaré with the snake, the Cuban near-absence"),
 ("yoruba","egungun","The Egungun","the masked ancestors who return, the costumes that must not touch the living, the Oyo Egungun festival and its policing role, the Egungun of Bahia (Itaparica), the Egungun as Oya's children"),
 ("yoruba","iyami_aje","The Iyami Aje","the 'our mothers', the witches as a power, the Gelede masquerade that placates them, the bird, the ambivalence of aje, the witchcraft accusations and the colonial trials, the modern feminist reading"),
 ("yoruba","ori","Ori","the head as personal god and destiny, chosen before birth at Ajala's house, the ibori shrine, the Ifá verses on Ori as the only orisha who follows one everywhere, the Cuban Orí (Eledá) and the rogación de cabeza"),
 ("yoruba","odu_ifa","The 256 Odu of Ifá","the sixteen major and 240 minor signs as beings, Odu the woman who owned Ifá and gave it to Orunmila (the Ifá verse), the binary structure and its geomantic cousins (the Arabic raml, the Malagasy sikidy), the Odu as the orisha's mother, the Iyanifa question"),
 ("yoruba","orisha_oko","Orisha Oko","the farm god of the harvest and the new yam, the iron staff, the judge of witches at Irawo, Orisha Oko in Cuba (St Isidore) with the oxen and the tiles"),
 ("yoruba","yewa","Yewa","the virgin of the cemetery, the river Yewa, Yewá in Cuba (the graveyard, the prohibition on sex for her children) and the Brazilian Ewá of the mist and the ophidian"),
 ("yoruba","erinle","Erinle (Inle)","the hunter-healer of the river Erinle, the fish, Inle of Cuba (St Raphael, the physician, the patron of gay men and the Inle-Abbata pair), the Brazilian Logun Edé's father"),
 ("yoruba","logun_ede","Logun Edé","the son of Oshosi and Oshun, half the year male hunter and half female of the waters, the Brazilian orisha of the Ketu nation and the modern queer reading, the near-absence in Yorubaland"),
 ("yoruba","dada","Dada (Bayanni)","the child orisha of the curly hair and the crown of cowries, Shango's brother or guardian, the Cuban Dadá and the Brazilian Baiani"),
 ("yoruba","oke","Oke","the mountain orisha of Ibadan and Abeokuta (the Olumo rock), the hill cults and their shrines, Oke in Cuba as a road of Obatala"),
 ("yoruba","iroko","Iroko","the tree as orisha (Milicia excelsa), the sacrifices at its foot, the Cuban Iroko as the ceiba and the Brazilian Tempo/Loko of the Jeje nation, the Dahomean Loko"),
 ("yoruba","ajogun","The Ajogun","the warriors against man (death, disease, loss, paralysis, big trouble, curse, imprisonment, affliction), the eight in Ifá, Eshu as their go-between, the sacrifices that turn them"),
 ("yoruba","osun_staff","Osun (the staff of Ifá)","the iron staff with the bird that stands for the babalawo's life, distinct from the goddess Oshun (say so at the top), the Osun in Cuba as one of the Warriors received with Elegguá, Ogún and Ochosi"),
 # ---------------- VODOU ----------------
 ("vodou","bondye","Bondye","the distant good God of Haitian Vodou (Bon Dieu), the Catholic overlay and the Fon Mawu behind him, 'Bondye bon', why the lwa are served and he is not, the Vodou theology debates (Hurbon, Desmangles)"),
 ("vodou","papa_legba","Papa Legba","the old man at the gate with the crutch and the dog, the first invoked, the Fon Legba (the phallic trickster of the Dahomean crossroads) and his Haitian aging, Legba and St Peter and St Lazarus, the Petro Legba, the blues crossroads legend (Robert Johnson) as a documented modern confusion"),
 ("vodou","damballa","Damballa","the great serpent of the sky and the springs, the Dahomean Dan/Dangbe (the Ouidah python temple), the white eggs and the tree, St Patrick's snakes, the possession that does not speak, Damballa in the New Orleans lore (Li Grand Zombi)"),
 ("vodou","ayida_wedo","Ayida-Wedo","the rainbow serpent, Damballa's wife, the Dahomean Aido-Hwedo who carries the world, the rainbow and the marriage, the Yoruba Osumare as cognate"),
 ("vodou","erzulie_freda","Erzulie Freda","the lwa of love, luxury and tears, the Mater Dolorosa image, the three rings, the perfumes and the weeping at the end of possession, the Fon origins (Azili), Deren's portrait, the gay men's patroness"),
 ("vodou","erzulie_dantor","Erzulie Dantor","the black Madonna of Częstochowa with the scars, the fierce mother, the knife, the mute tongue, the Bois Caïman association (the possessed priestess of 1791 and the historiography), the lesbian patroness, the Petro Erzulie"),
 ("vodou","baron_samedi","Baron Samedi","the lord of the dead in top hat and tails at the cemetery cross, the first man buried, the obscenity and the rum with peppers, the Barons (La Croix, Cimetière, Kriminel), Duvalier's use of the image (the sunglasses and the tonton macoutes), the James Bond Baron as reception"),
 ("vodou","maman_brigitte","Maman Brigitte","the Baron's wife, the only white lwa, the first woman buried, St Brigid and the Irish and Scottish indentured of Saint-Domingue as the theory of her origin, the cemetery's black rooster"),
 ("vodou","gede","The Gede","the family of the dead as clowning lwa, Papa Gede, Gede Nibo, the November festival, the sexual jokes and the sunglasses with one lens, the Gede as healers of children, the Gede of the Cité Soleil"),
 ("vodou","ogou","Ogou","the warrior lwa of iron and the machete, Ogou Feray, Ogou Badagri, Ogou Balendjo, St James the Greater on horseback, Dessalines as Ogou, the rum and the red, the Yoruba Ogun as source, the politics of Ogou in Haitian history"),
 ("vodou","agwe","Agwe","the admiral of the sea, the boat set adrift as offering (the bark of Agwe), the conch, St Ulrich with the fish, La Sirène as his consort, the sailors and the boat people"),
 ("vodou","la_sirene","La Sirène","the mermaid of the sea with the mirror and comb, the trumpet, the Mami Wata of West Africa and the Yemoja/Iemanjá parallel, the Stella Maris image, the singers as her children"),
 ("vodou","loko","Loko","the lwa of the trees and the priesthood, the Dahomean Loko (the iroko tree), the first houngan, the leaves and the asson's origin, St Joseph"),
 ("vodou","ayizan","Ayizan","the first mambo, the market and the palm fronds of initiation (the kanzo), the Dahomean Ayizan of the market gates, the shredded palm as her sign, the lwa of purity"),
 ("vodou","simbi","Simbi","the water snakes of the springs and the magic, Simbi Andezo, Simbi Makaya, the Kongo simbi spirits as source, the guardian of the sorcerers and the Three Kings, the 'Simbi in the rain'"),
 ("vodou","marassa","The Marassa","the divine twins who precede the lwa, the Dahomean Hoho and the Yoruba Ibeji, the three (Marassa Twa), the children's plates, Cosmas and Damian, the twins' power to heal and to harm"),
 ("vodou","azaka","Azaka (Kouzen Zaka)","the peasant lwa in the straw hat and denim with the makout bag, the Ministry of Agriculture's cousin, the stinginess and the pipe, St Isidore, the Petro Azaka"),
 ("vodou","bossou","Bossou","the bull lwa with the three horns, the Dahomean royal bull (King Tegbesu's Bossou Ashadeh), the wild and the tame, Bossou in the Petro rites"),
 ("vodou","kalfou","Kalfou (Carrefour)","the Petro master of the crossroads, Legba's dark double, the sorcerers' gate, the midnight and the red, the Kalfou of the secret societies (Bizango, Sanpwel)"),
 ("vodou","ti_jean_petro","Ti Jean Petro","the one-legged fire lwa in the trees, the Petro rite's origin in Don Pedro (the Spaniard? the slave? the 1768 dance banned by the French), the pepper and the whip, Ti Jean Dantor"),
 ("vodou","gran_bwa","Gran Bwa","the master of the forest and the leaves, the initiation in the woods, the tree-man image, St Sebastian, the herbal knowledge"),
 ("vodou","sobo_and_bade","Sobo and Bade","the thunder and the wind, the Dahomean Hevioso's Haitian form, the general in uniform, the lightning stones"),
 ("vodou","agassou","Agassou","the leopard ancestor of the Dahomean kings (the princess and the leopard), the lwa of the Abomey lineage in Haiti, the crab and the claw-hand, the royal Fon origin of the Rada rite"),
 ("vodou","mawu_lisa","Mawu-Lisa","the Dahomean moon-sun creator pair, the children of Nana Buluku, the sixteen children and the vodun as their offices, the Fon cosmogony (Herskovits, Mercier), the Bondye behind the Haitian God"),
 ("vodou","gu","Gu","the Fon iron and war god, the Yoruba Ogun's Dahomean form, the Gu statue of the Musée du quai Branly (the iron warrior from Ouidah, 1858), the Ogou of Haiti as his heir"),
 ("vodou","sakpata","Sakpata","the Fon earth and smallpox vodun, the king's rival ('the second king'), the Sakpata cult's ban under Agaja and its return, the Yoruba Shopona and the Haitian Azaka's earth"),
 ("vodou","hevioso","Hevioso (Xevioso)","the Fon thunder vodun with the ram and the axe, the So of the Hevie shrine, the Yoruba Shango as cognate, the Haitian Sobo"),
 ("vodou","dan","Dan (Dangbe)","the Fon serpent vodun, the rainbow and the python of Ouidah's temple (the Portuguese and the Brazilian visitors), Dan as the principle of movement and wealth, Damballa and Ayida as his Haitian halves"),
 ("vodou","new_orleans_voodoo","New Orleans Voodoo (the spirits)","the Louisiana branch as a system: Li Grand Zombi, Papa Lébat, the St John's Eve rituals on Bayou St John, the Congo Square dances, Marie Laveau's cult (as reception of a person), the gris-gris and the hoodoo distinction, Tallant's inventions, the tourist Voodoo of today"),
 ("vodou","petro_lwa","The Petro rite and its lwa","the hot rite beside the Rada: the whip, the gunpowder, the Kongo and Creole origins, the Don Pedro dance of 1768, the Petro nation's lwa as a group (Erzulie Dantor, Kalfou, Ti Jean, Marinette, Simbi Makaya, Bossou), the Bois Caïman question, the secret societies"),
 # ---------------- MAPUCHE ----------------
 ("mapuche","ngunechen","Ngünechen (Ngenechén)","the ruler of the people, the four-fold old man, old woman, young man, young woman, the nguillatun addressed to him, the Christian shaping of the name (Foerster's argument), the Chau/Futa Chao names, the debate whether a pre-contact supreme god existed"),
 ("mapuche","pillan","Pillan","the volcano spirits and the ancestors' thunder, the pillan of the caciques after death, the Spaniards' 'devil' Pillan, the Pillan of the Villarrica and Llaima eruptions, the pillanes as a class and as a god"),
 ("mapuche","antu","Antü","the sun as father and the Antü of the four-fold god, the sun-worship reports of the chroniclers, the We Tripantu (winter solstice) and the sun's return, the kultrun's painted sun"),
 ("mapuche","kuyen","Küyen","the moon as mother and mistress of women, the menstrual and planting calendar, the Küyen of the machi's kultrun, the moon-sun marriage myths"),
 ("mapuche","kai_kai_and_tren_tren","Kai-Kai Vilu and Tren-Tren Vilu","the sea serpent and the earth serpent, the flood and the rising mountain, the survivors turned to fish and the four elders, the versions (Rosales 1674 as the earliest, Koessler-Ilg, the Chiloé forms), the 1960 Valdivia earthquake and the reported sacrifice at Collileufu (the trial), the myth as the founding story of the Mapuche"),
 ("mapuche","ngen","The Ngen","the owners of nature (ngen-ko of the waters, ngen-mapu of the land, ngen-winkul of the hills, ngen-kütral of fire, ngen-mawida of the forest), the permission asked before taking, Grebe's ethnography, the Ngen in the current environmental conflicts (the hydroelectric dams, Ralco)"),
 ("mapuche","wekufe","Wekufe (Huecuve)","the evil spirit and the class of harm-bringers, the disease as wekufe, the kalku's servants, the Spaniards' equation with the Devil and its adoption, the Wekufe of the machi's diagnosis"),
 ("mapuche","anchimallen","Anchimallen (Anchimayén)","the little shining spirit or the kalku's ball of fire, the child-sized companion, the light that follows travellers, Chiloé's and Neuquén's versions"),
 ("mapuche","cherufe","Cherufe","the lava monster of the volcanoes who eats maidens, the fireballs and meteorites, the sacrifice legends, the Chilean Cherufe of the school readers and its Mapuche basis"),
 ("mapuche","chonchon","Chonchón","the flying head with ears for wings, the kalku transformed, the 'tue tue' cry, the Chilote and Argentine versions, the countermeasures"),
 ("mapuche","colo_colo","Colo Colo","the rat-serpent hatched from a rooster's egg that drinks the sleeper's saliva, the basilisk parallel (Chiloé's basilisco), the football club's name as reception (Colo Colo the toqui is a person)"),
 ("mapuche","peuchen","Peuchén (Piuchén)","the flying snake that whistles and drains blood, the shape-shifter, the paralysing gaze, the Piuchén of Chiloé and the machi's remedies"),
 ("mapuche","invunche","Invunche (Imbunche)","the deformed guardian of the warlocks' cave with the twisted head and the leg sewn to the back, the kidnapped child, the Chilote brujos of Quicaví and the 1880 trial of the Recta Provincia, Donoso's El obsceno pájaro de la noche as reception"),
 ("mapuche","trauco","The Trauco","the small forest man of Chiloé with the stone axe and the gaze that twists, the seducer blamed for pregnancies, his wife the Fiura, the Trauco of the tourist Chiloé"),
 ("mapuche","pincoya","The Pincoya","the sea woman who dances on the beach to bring or deny the shellfish, facing the sea or the land, Millalobo's daughter, the drowned sailors carried to the Caleuche, the Pincoya of Chiloé's fishermen"),
 ("mapuche","caleuche","The Caleuche","the ghost ship of Chiloé with lights and music, the brujos' vessel, the transformed drowned, the sightings in the channels, the Flying Dutchman comparison and the Chilote specificity"),
 ("mapuche","millalobo","Millalobo","the king of the sea of Chiloé, half man half seal, born of a woman and a sea lion after the great flood, father of the Pincoya, the Sirena Chilota and the Pincoy, the ruler of the fishing"),
 ("mapuche","sumpall","Sumpall","the water spirit who takes the girls at the rivers and lakes, the marriage with the Sumpall and the bride-price of fish, the Mapuche water-being of the Araucanía lakes (Koessler-Ilg, Augusta)"),
 ("mapuche","nguru_filu","Ngürü-filu (the fox-snake)","the river monster half fox half serpent that overturns boats, the Ngürüvilu of the river crossings, the machi's exorcism"),
 ("mapuche","camahueto","Camahueto","the one-horned calf of Chiloé that grows in the rivers and tears the land to the sea, the horn shavings as remedy, the machi who catches it with a lasso of sargazo"),
 ("mapuche","cuero","Cuero (Trelquehuecuve)","the living hide in the water that wraps and drinks its prey, the eyes on the rim, the thorns as defence, the Manta of the Chilean lakes"),
 ("mapuche","kalku","The Kalku","the witch or sorcerer as a class, the opposite of the machi, the Chilote brujos (the Recta Provincia and the 1880 trial), the wekufe and the invunche as their tools, the modern accusations"),
 ("mapuche","machi_spirits","The Machi's spirits (the filew)","the machi's tutelary spirits and the rewe, the machi's calling (the perimontun), the kultrun, the machitun and the ascent, Bacigalupo's Shamans of the Foye Tree, the machi in the current politics"),
 ("mapuche","elal","Elal (Tehuelche)","the Tehuelche culture hero born of the giant Nóshtex and the cloud Teo, raised by the swan and the rodent, the inventor of fire and the bow, the flight to the sky from the sea, the Tehuelche of Santa Cruz as Patagonia's other people (Bórmida and Siffredi, Lista's Los indios tehuelches), placed here as the neighbour"),
 ("mapuche","selknam_spirits","The Selk'nam (Ona) spirits: Temáukel and the Hain","Temáukel the distant supreme being, Kénos the shaper, the Hain initiation and its spirits (Shoort, Xalpen, Kulan, the Sun and Moon myth of the women's lodge), Gusinde's Die Feuerland-Indianer, Chapman's Drama and Power in a Hunting Society, the 1923 Hain photographs, the genocide, placed here as the Fuegian neighbour"),
