 ("guarani","tupa","Tupã","the thunder as the Guaraní's god, the Jesuits' choice of Tupã for the Christian God (Montoya) and what that did to him, the Tupinambá Tupan of Léry and Thevet, Tupã in the Mbyá cosmogony as one of the four (Cadogan), the Brazilian Tupã of the Romantic Indianism (Gonçalves Dias)"),
