 ("guarani","tau_and_kerana","Tau and Kerana","the evil spirit who abducted Kerana, the daughter of Marangatu, and fathered the seven monsters, the curse of Arasy, Colmán's 1929 systematization and the older oral material behind it, the seven as the folkloric canon of Paraguay and Corrientes"),
 ("guarani","teju_jagua","Teju Jagua","the lizard with seven dog heads, the first of the seven monsters, the guardian of caves and the fruit, the fiery eyes, the hidden treasures"),
 ("guarani","mboi_tui","Mbói Tu'i","the serpent-parrot, the second, the guardian of the waters and the wetlands, the cry that terrifies"),
 ("guarani","monai","Moñái","the horned serpent of the fields who hypnotises birds and steals, the third, defeated by Porâsý's sacrifice, the thieves' patron"),
 ("guarani","jasy_jatere","Jasy Jateré","the small blond man with the golden staff who takes children at siesta, the fourth, the honey and the forest, the Pombero comparison, the siesta warnings of Paraguay and Corrientes, the Yasy Yateré of the Argentine northeast"),
 ("guarani","kurupi","Kurupí","the forest man with the coiled phallus, the fifth, the protector of the wild and the seducer, the pregnancies blamed on him, the Kurupí carvings of the Chaco and the crafts"),
 ("guarani","ao_ao","Ao Ao","the sheep-like monster with the terrible cry that hunts men in packs, the sixth, the pindo palm that saves, the protector of hills"),
 ("guarani","luison","Luisón","the seventh son as the dog of death at the cemeteries, the seventh monster, the werewolf overlay (lobizón) and the Argentine presidential godparenting of seventh sons (the 1907 origin, the 1973 law), the Friday night transformation"),
 ("guarani","pombero","The Pombero","the hairy little man of the night who whistles, the tobacco and caña left for him, the friendship and the revenge, the pregnancies, Villafañe and the Corrientes and Misiones lore, the Pombero of the Argentine popular culture"),
 ("guarani","angatupyry","Angatupyry","the good spirit, the counterpart of Taú, the guardian and inspirer of good, the moral dualism of the folkloric cosmogony and its Christian shaping"),
 ("guarani","pora","Pora (Póra)","the ghost or apparition, the soul in pain, the pora of the abandoned houses and the treasures, the Corrientes and Misiones pora stories, the word's spread into Argentine Spanish"),
 ("guarani","kaa_jaryi","Ka'a Jarýi","the owner of the yerba mate, the goddess of the yerbales, the yerba mate origin myths (the moon's gift, the old man's hospitality), the mensú and the yerbales of Misiones as her domain, Ka'a Pora"),
 ("guarani","pai_sume","Pa'i Sumé (Sumé)","the culture hero who taught the yerba mate and agriculture and left his footprints, the Jesuits' identification with St Thomas the Apostle (Nóbrega, Montoya) and the footprints of São Tomé, the Tupinambá Sumé, the Mbyá Pa'i Rete Kuaray comparison"),
 ("guarani","yvy_mara_ey","Yvy Marã Ey (the Land Without Evil)","the land where the corn grows alone and there is no death, the Tupí-Guaraní migrations toward it (the 16th-century movements to the coast and to Peru, Nimuendajú's Apapokuva of 1912), Hélène Clastres's book, the prophets (karai) who led them, the modern Guaraní and the concept's politics"),
 ("guarani","nande_sy","Ñande Sy (the First Mother)","the mother of the twins eaten by the jaguars (the primordial jaguars), her bones and her return, the Mbyá and Kaiowá versions of the twin cycle, the Ñande Sy of the Kaiowá as the mother of the maize"),
 ("guarani","guarani_twins","The Guaraní Twins (Pa'i Kuaray and Jasy)","the twin cycle as one dossier: the mother eaten, the twins' revenge on the jaguars, the recovery of the mother's bones, the ascent as sun and moon, Nimuendajú's Apapokuva text, Métraux, the comparanda in the Tupí and in the Andes"),
 # ---------------- GNOSTIC ----------------
 ("gnostic","pleroma_thirty_aeons","The Pleroma (the thirty aeons)","the Valentinian fullness as one dossier: the Ogdoad, Decad and Dodecad of Irenaeus I.1-3 (Ptolemy's system), the syzygies, the names of all thirty, the variant lists (Hippolytus, the Tripartite Tractate's unnumbered aeons), the passion of the last aeon and the fall, the Sethian contrast, the number thirty and the parable of the vineyard"),
 ("gnostic","bythos","Bythos (Depth, the Propator)","the unbegotten first principle of Ptolemy's Valentinianism, the Forefather in silence, Irenaeus I.1.1, the Bythos of the Marcosians and the letters, the relation to the Sethian Invisible Spirit"),
 ("gnostic","sige_ennoia","Sige / Ennoia (Silence, Thought)","the consort of Bythos, Silence who is also Thought and Grace, the mother of Nous and Aletheia, the Simonian Ennoia (Helena, Simon Magus's companion as the fallen Thought, Irenaeus I.23) as the earlier form, the Barbelo comparison"),
 ("gnostic","nous_monogenes","Nous (Monogenes, the Only-begotten)","the first emitted aeon who alone knows the Father, the Mind, Monogenes and Arche, the father of Logos and Zoe, Irenaeus I.1.1, the Johannine Monogenes reading, the Nous of Poimandres as the Hermetic form"),
 ("gnostic","aletheia_aeon","Aletheia (Truth)","the consort of Nous, the first tetrad's completion, Truth in the Gospel of Truth and the Tripartite Tractate, the Marcosian Aletheia with the letters on her body (Irenaeus I.14), the body of Truth as the alphabet"),
 ("gnostic","logos_aeon","Logos (the aeon)","the Word as the fifth aeon, son of Nous and Aletheia, the Logos of the Tripartite Tractate who falls and is restored (the Valentinian version of Sophia's fall), the Johannine Logos and the Valentinian commentary on John (Heracleon, Ptolemy's letter)"),
 ("gnostic","zoe_aeon","Zoe (Life)","the consort of Logos, Life in the Ogdoad, the Zoe of On the Origin of the World who is Eve's spiritual double (Eve-Zoe, the instructor), the tree of life and the serpent, the Epinoia identification"),
 ("gnostic","anthropos_aeon","Anthropos (the aeon Man)","the heavenly Man, son of Logos and Zoe, the Anthropos of Poimandres who fell in love with Nature, the Adamas of the Sethians, the primal Man of the Naassenes (Hippolytus V), the Manichaean Primal Man (own file), the Adam Kadmon comparison"),
 ("gnostic","ekklesia_aeon","Ekklesia (the aeon Church)","the consort of Anthropos, the Church pre-existent in the Pleroma, the completion of the Ogdoad, the Valentinian ecclesiology and the spiritual seed"),
 ("gnostic","achamoth","Achamoth","the lower Sophia expelled from the Pleroma, formless until Horos and Christ shape her, the mother of the Demiurge and of the psychic and material from her passions, Irenaeus I.4-5, the Hebrew hokhmah behind the name, the Achamoth of the Excerpta ex Theodoto"),
 ("gnostic","horos_stauros","Horos (Limit, Stauros)","the aeon Limit who separates the Pleroma from what fell, also called Stauros (Cross), Irenaeus I.2.4, the Horos of the Excerpta, the cross as boundary and the Valentinian reading of the crucifixion"),
 ("gnostic","christ_aeon","Christ (the aeon) and the Holy Spirit","the pair emitted after Sophia's fall to teach the aeons the Father's incomprehensibility, Irenaeus I.2.5-6, the distinction from Jesus-Soter the fruit of the Pleroma, the several Christs of the Valentinian systems, Clement's Excerpta on the descent"),
 ("gnostic","jesus_soter","Jesus the Saviour (Soter, the fruit of the Pleroma)","the common fruit of all the aeons, the Saviour who shapes Achamoth and the psychic Christ who descends on Jesus, the Valentinian docetism and its varieties, the Gospel of Truth's Jesus, the Excerpta's Jesus, the Naassene Jesus"),
 ("gnostic","ogdoad_gnostic","The Ogdoad (the eighth heaven)","the eighth as the sphere of the fixed stars above the seven planetary archons (Irenaeus I.5.2, I.30; Hippolytus VII on Basilides; the Discourse on the Eighth and Ninth; Corpus Hermeticum I.24-26), the Ogdoad as Sophia's dwelling and the middle place, the eight aeons of the Valentinian Ogdoad as a different sense, the Ogdoad of Hermopolis as a third (egyptian/ogdoad.md), the number eight (Clement Stromateis VI.16), the 888 of Jesus (Irenaeus I.15.2); the Colegio's essays use this sense, one line"),
 ("gnostic","saklas","Saklas","the Fool, the name of the demiurge in the Sethian texts (the Apocryphon of John, the Gospel of the Egyptians, the Gospel of Judas where Saklas rules with Nebro), the three names (Yaldabaoth, Saklas, Samael), the Saklas of Manichaeism as the archon who made Adam"),
 ("gnostic","sabaoth","Sabaoth (the repentant archon)","the son of Yaldabaoth who repented and was raised to the seventh heaven with a chariot and the cherubim (the Hypostasis of the Archons, On the Origin of the World), the Lord of Hosts reinterpreted, the Sabaoth of the PGM and the gems, the Zoe who instructed him"),
 ("gnostic","nebro","Nebro (Yaldabaoth of the Gospel of Judas)","the rebel angel with the face of fire and blood, the Gospel of Judas's cosmogony (Tchacos codex, 2006), the twelve angels and the birth of Saklas, the Nebro-Yaldabaoth equation, the Gospel of Judas controversy (the 'demon' Judas reading of DeConick)"),
 ("gnostic","autogenes","Autogenes (the Self-begotten)","the third member of the Sethian triad (Invisible Spirit, Barbelo, Autogenes), the divine Christ of the Apocryphon of John, the Four Luminaries as his attendants, the Autogenes of Zostrianos and Allogenes, the Sethian baptism"),
 ("gnostic","four_luminaries","The Four Luminaries (Harmozel, Oroiael, Daveithai, Eleleth)","the four lights of the Sethian Pleroma with their twelve aeons, the dwellings of Adamas, Seth, the seed of Seth and the repentant, Eleleth who sent Norea help and (in the Trimorphic Protennoia) whose word produced the demiurge, the Gospel of the Egyptians, the Apocryphon of John"),
 ("gnostic","seth_heavenly","Seth (the heavenly Seth, the Great Seth)","the son of Adamas in the Pleroma and the father of the immovable race, the Second Treatise of the Great Seth, the Three Steles of Seth, the Gospel of the Egyptians (Seth incarnate as Jesus), the Sethians as named by Hippolytus and Epiphanius, the Seth of the Manichaeans and the Mandaean Shitil, Turner's Sethian Gnosticism"),
 ("gnostic","norea","Norea","the daughter of Eve and wife of Noah (or Seth), who burned the ark and called to the heights, the Hypostasis of the Archons and the Thought of Norea, the Naamah of Genesis 4:22 and the Jewish legends behind her, Epiphanius's Noria of the Nicolaitans, the archons' assault and Eleleth's rescue"),
