 ("gnostic","epinoia","Epinoia (the Epinoia of Light)","the afterthought of light sent to Adam as his helper, hidden in him, the Eve of light and the tree of knowledge, the Apocryphon of John's Epinoia and the Zoe of On the Origin of the World, the Pronoia/Epinoia pair, the female saviour figure"),
 ("gnostic","poimandres","Poimandres","the Mind of the Sovereignty who reveals the cosmogony to Hermes in Corpus Hermeticum I, the name's Egyptian etymology (Kitchen: p-eime n-re, the knowledge of Re) and the Greek 'shepherd of men' reading, the Anthropos and Nature, the ascent through the seven spheres to the Ogdoad, Ficino's translation of 1463 and the Renaissance Pimander, the Colegio's essays in one line"),
 ("gnostic","invisible_spirit","The Invisible Spirit (the Monad)","the Sethian first principle beyond being, the Apocryphon of John's negative theology (the Monad, 'not perfect, more than perfect'), Allogenes and Zostrianos on the Triple-Powered One, the relation to Plotinus's One and the Gnostics he refuted (Ennead II.9)"),
 ("gnostic","hibil_ziwa","Hibil Ziwa (Mandaean)","the Mandaean saviour who descends to the world of darkness, the Ginza Rabba's account of his descent and return, Hibil as Abel, the Mandaeans of Iraq and Iran (Drower, Buckley) and the diaspora after 2003, the baptism (masbuta) and the living water"),
 ("gnostic","ruha_mandaean","Ruha (Mandaean)","the Spirit as the female ruler of the world of darkness, the mother of the seven planets and the twelve signs by Ur, the Ruha d-Qudsha inverted, the Ginza and the Book of John, Buckley's reading of Ruha's ambiguity and repentance"),
 ("gnostic","ptahil","Ptahil (Mandaean)","the Mandaean demiurge who formed the earth and the body of Adam with the help of the dark powers, the son of Abathur, the Ptahil of the Ginza's cosmogony and his eventual redemption, the name's Egyptian Ptah debate, Abathur and his scales as the judge"),
 ("gnostic","primal_man_manichaean","The Primal Man (Manichaean)","the First Man sent by the Father of Greatness to fight the darkness, armed with his five sons the elements, defeated and swallowed, rescued by the Living Spirit's call, the Kephalaia and the Fihrist, the Manichaean Adam Kadmon comparison, the Ohrmizd of the Iranian Manichaean texts"),
 ("gnostic","living_spirit_manichaean","The Living Spirit (Manichaean)","the second emanation who rescues the Primal Man and builds the cosmos from the bodies of the archons (the ten heavens and eight earths), the Mihryazd of the Iranian texts, the Call and the Answer, the Manichaean demiurge who is good"),
 ("gnostic","third_messenger_manichaean","The Third Messenger (Manichaean)","the Tertius Legatus who displays his beauty to the archons so they release the light in their seed (the seduction of the archons), the sun and moon as ships of light, the Column of Glory, Augustine's scandalized account (De natura boni), Narisah of the Iranian texts"),
 ("gnostic","king_of_darkness_manichaean","The King of Darkness (Manichaean)","the Prince of the realm of darkness with five worlds and the five-shaped body (demon, lion, eagle, fish, dragon), the invasion of the light, the Hyle of the Greek texts and the Ahriman of the Iranian, the Kephalaia's description, the Manichaean dualism's later career (the Paulicians, Bogomils and Cathars as reception, disputed)"),
