 ("celtic","aengus","Aengus (Óengus mac Óg)","the young son of the Dagda and Boann conceived and born in a single stretched day, the winning of the Brú by a trick of words, the Dream of Óengus (Aislinge Óenguso) and Caer the swan, the fosterer of Diarmuid, the birds around his head, the Yeats poem"),
