 ("celtic","ogma","Ogma","the champion of the Tuatha Dé, the inventor of ogham (the Auraicept and In Lebor Ogaim), the honey-mouthed, the Gaulish Ogmios of Lucian's Hercules with the chains from his tongue, the Ogmios-Ogma link and its problems"),
 ("celtic","balor","Balor","the Fomorian with the destroying eye, the prophecy of the grandson, Eithne in the tower, killed by Lugh's sling-stone at Mag Tuired, the Tory Island folklore versions, the Balor of the Irish oral tradition (Larminie, Curtin)"),
 ("celtic","bres","Bres","the beautiful half-Fomorian king of the Tuatha Dé who was stingy and satirized (the first satire in Ireland, Cairbre's), the Cath Maige Tuired's account, the knowledge of ploughing and sowing given for his life, the bad king as a type"),
