 ("aztec","xochiquetzal","Xochiquetzal","the flower-quetzal goddess of love, beauty and the crafts, the wife stolen by Tezcatlipoca, the patroness of the ahuianime, the Toci relation, the first woman of the Histoyre du Mechique"),
 ("aztec","xochipilli","Xochipilli","the flower prince of song, games and pleasure, the statue from Tlalmanalco with the hallucinogenic flowers carved on it (Wasson's reading), Macuilxochitl and the Ahuiateteo, the patolli"),
 ("aztec","chalchiuhtlicue","Chalchiuhtlicue","the jade skirt, the goddess of lakes and rivers and Tlaloc's consort, the sun of the fourth age that ended in flood, the baptism of infants in her name, the Teotihuacan Great Goddess question"),
 ("aztec","huehueteotl","Huehueteotl (Xiuhtecuhtli)","the old god of fire with the brazier on his head, the oldest deity of Mesoamerica (Cuicuilco), the Xiuhtecuhtli of the year and the turquoise, the New Fire ceremony every 52 years on the Hill of the Star (1507 the last), the centre of the world"),
 ("aztec","ometeotl","Ometeotl (Ometecuhtli and Omecihuatl)","the dual god of Omeyocan, the parents of the four Tezcatlipocas, León-Portilla's Ometeotl as the supreme principle and the critique (Haly: a modern construction from thin sources), the Tonacatecuhtli pair"),
 ("aztec","mixcoatl","Mixcoatl","the cloud serpent, the hunter god of the Chichimecs with the stars' paint, the father of Quetzalcoatl by Chimalman, the Quecholli festival's hunt, the four hundred Mimixcoa, the Camaxtli of Tlaxcala"),
 ("aztec","cihuacoatl","Cihuacoatl","the snake woman, the mother goddess who wails in the night (the omen before the conquest, the Llorona's ancestor), the title of the Mexica's second ruler (Tlacaelel), the Cihuateteo the women dead in childbirth as her host, the Tonantzin relation and Guadalupe"),
 ("aztec","tlaltecuhtli","Tlaltecuhtli","the earth monster torn in two by Quetzalcoatl and Tezcatlipoca to make sky and earth, the mouths at the joints, the carvings on the undersides of sculptures, the 12-ton monolith found in 2006 at the Templo Mayor, the earth that eats the dead"),
