 ("aztec","mayahuel","Mayahuel","the maguey goddess with four hundred breasts for the four hundred rabbits (the Centzon Totochtin, the pulque gods), the maiden brought down from the sky by Quetzalcoatl and torn by the Tzitzimime, the pulque's origin, the Codex Borgia image"),
 ("aztec","xolotl","Xolotl","the dog-headed twin of Quetzalcoatl who guided the dead and the sun through the underworld, the god of deformity and the evening star, the axolotl who hid from sacrifice, the ballgame's patron"),
 ("aztec","ehecatl","Ehecatl","the wind aspect of Quetzalcoatl with the buccal mask, the round temples (Calixtlahuaca, the Mexico City metro's Pino Suárez temple), the wind that swept the road for the rain, the breath of life blown into the dead bones"),
 ("aztec","chantico","Chantico","the goddess of the hearth fire and of the goldsmiths' furnace, the fire in the house, the turning into a dog for breaking a fast, the Xochimilco cult"),
 ("aztec","tzitzimime","The Tzitzimime","the star demons of the darkness who will descend at the end of the fifth sun to devour mankind, feared at eclipses and at the New Fire, the skeletal women with the star-skirts, the Magliabechiano image, the Tzitzimitl as also a childbirth protector (the ambivalence)"),
 ("aztec","centeotl","Centeotl","the maize god, the son of Tlazolteotl, the maize's four colours, the Huey Tozoztli festival, the maize god of Teotihuacan and the Maya as comparison, the Chicomecoatl pair"),
