 ("aztec","tonantzin","Tonantzin","our revered mother as a title of the earth goddesses at Tepeyac, Sahagún's complaint that the Indians called the Virgin of Guadalupe Tonantzin, the continuity debate (Lafaye's Quetzalcóatl and Guadalupe, Poole's critique), the Guadalupe cult as reception"),
 ("aztec","tepeyollotl","Tepeyollotl","the heart of the mountain, the jaguar god of echoes and earthquakes, a form of Tezcatlipoca, the Borgia group's night lord, the caves"),
 ("aztec","itztlacoliuhqui","Itztlacoliuhqui","the curved obsidian blade, the god of frost, cold and blindness, the Tonatiuh struck by the arrow of the dawn and turned to stone, the justice of the blindfold, the Borbonicus image"),
 ("aztec","tlahuizcalpantecuhtli","Tlahuizcalpantecuhtli","the lord of the dawn, Venus as morning star, the dangerous rays that strike the old, the children and the maize on particular days (the Borgia Venus tables), the Quetzalcoatl who became the morning star after the pyre"),
 ("aztec","yacatecuhtli","Yacatecuhtli","the nose lord, the god of the pochteca merchants, the staff bundle worshipped on the road, the merchants' secret feasts and the slave sacrifices at Tlatelolco, the pochteca as spies"),
 ("aztec","opochtli","Opochtli","the left-handed god of the lake fishermen and fowlers of Tenochtitlan, the inventor of the net, the atlatl and the pole, the Tlaloque's kin, the lake economy's god"),
 ("aztec","patecatl","Patecatl","the lord of the pulque root and of medicine, Mayahuel's husband, the four hundred rabbits' father, the day-sign patron"),
 ("aztec","centzon_totochtin","The Centzon Totochtin (the Four Hundred Rabbits)","the pulque gods of drunkenness, Tepoztecatl of Tepoztlan and his pyramid, Ometochtli (Two Rabbit), the moon's rabbit, the drunk as 'a rabbit', the Tepoztlan festival today"),
 ("aztec","cihuateteo","The Cihuateteo","the women who died in first childbirth, deified as warriors who accompany the sun from noon to sunset, the crossroads shrines and the days they descend to steal children, the Cihuateotl sculptures, the Llorona and Guadalupe echoes"),
 ("aztec","tlaloque","The Tlaloque","the rain god's helpers who pour from the jars and break them for thunder, the four directions' Tlaloque, the mountain gods (Tepictoton) and the amaranth figures, the child sacrifices on the mountains"),
 ("aztec","ahuiateteo","The Ahuiateteo (the Macuiltonaleque)","the five gods of pleasure and excess (Macuilxochitl, Macuilcuetzpalin, Macuilcozcacuauhtli, Macuiltochtli, Macuilmalinalli), the Borgia images with the hand over the mouth, the punishments of excess (the venereal diseases), the games"),
 ("aztec","nanahuatzin","Nanahuatzin","the pustulent humble god who leapt first into the fire at Teotihuacan and became the sun while Tecciztecatl hesitated and became the moon (the rabbit thrown in his face), the Leyenda de los Soles, the humility as the Mexica ethos"),
 ("aztec","tecciztecatl","Tecciztecatl","the lord of the conch shell, the rich god who hesitated and became the moon, the rabbit's mark, the Florentine Codex's telling, the moon's gender in Aztec thought"),
 # ---------------- JAPANESE ----------------
 ("japanese","amaterasu","Amaterasu","the sun goddess born of Izanagi's left eye, the cave (Ama-no-Iwato) and the dance of Uzume and the mirror, the imperial ancestress and the Ise shrine (the rebuilding every twenty years), the Yata no Kagami, the Amaterasu of State Shinto and the 1946 renunciation, the Amaterasu of Kurozumikyō and the modern shrines"),
 ("japanese","susanoo","Susanoo","the storm god who ravaged the heavens and was expelled, the eight-headed Orochi killed at Izumo and the sword from its tail (Kusanagi), the Izumo cycle and the Kojiki-Nihon Shoki differences, the Korean Silla connection (Soshimori), the Gion cult and Gozu Tennō, the Susanoo of the Yasaka shrine"),
