 ("japanese","izanagi_and_izanami","Izanagi and Izanami","the creator pair who stirred the sea with the jewelled spear and made Onogoro, the marriage and the leech-child, the death of Izanami bearing fire, the descent to Yomi and the rotting body and the flight, the purification that bore the three children, the Awaji shrine, the Orpheus comparison"),
 ("japanese","inari","Inari","the rice god with the foxes, the Fushimi Inari shrine and its ten thousand torii (711), the male, female and androgynous Inari, the Buddhist Dakiniten fusion, the Inari of the merchants and the geisha, the 30,000 shrines, Smyers's The Fox and the Jewel"),
 ("japanese","hachiman","Hachiman","the god of war and of the Minamoto, the deified Emperor Ōjin (the identification's history), the Usa shrine and the oracle of 769 (Dōkyō), the Great Bodhisattva Hachiman as the first kami-Buddha fusion, the Iwashimizu and Tsurugaoka shrines, the samurai's god"),
