 ("japanese","ame_no_uzume","Ame-no-Uzume","the goddess of the dawn who danced half-naked on the overturned tub before the cave and made the gods laugh, the ancestress of the Sarume and of kagura, the confronting of Sarutahiko, the Otafuku face"),
 ("japanese","takemikazuchi","Takemikazuchi","the thunder and sword god who subdued Ōkuninushi's son in the sumo match on the beach of Inasa (the first sumo), the Kashima shrine and the keystone that holds the catfish Namazu (the earthquakes), the Fujiwara's god, the sword Futsunomitama"),
 ("japanese","ryujin","Ryūjin (Watatsumi)","the dragon king of the sea with the tide jewels, the palace under the sea (Ryūgū-jō), Hoori and Toyotama-hime, Urashima Tarō as reception, the Empress Jingū's jewels, the dragon kings of Buddhism as source"),
 ("japanese","kagutsuchi","Kagutsuchi","the fire god whose birth burned his mother Izanami, cut into pieces by Izanagi's sword and the gods born of his blood, the Atago and Akiba fire shrines, the Hi-no-kagutsuchi festivals against fire"),
 ("japanese","raijin_and_fujin","Raijin and Fūjin","the thunder god with the ring of drums and the wind god with the bag, the Sanjūsangendō statues and Sōtatsu's screens, the Buddhist Vajrapāni origins of the pair, the thunder that takes navels"),
 ("japanese","ebisu","Ebisu","the fisherman god with the sea bream and the rod, the only one of the Seven Lucky Gods born in Japan, the leech-child Hiruko as his origin (the identification's date), the Nishinomiya shrine, the god who stays home in the gods' month, the beer as reception"),
 ("japanese","daikokuten","Daikokuten","the Mahākāla of India made the god of wealth with the mallet and the rice bales, the Ōkuninushi fusion by the name's reading, the kitchen god of Saichō's Mount Hiei, the Seven Lucky Gods"),
 ("japanese","benzaiten","Benzaiten","the Sarasvatī of India made the goddess of music, eloquence and water, the biwa and the white snake, Enoshima, Chikubushima and Itsukushima, the Ugajin fusion with the snake-body, the only woman of the Seven"),
 ("japanese","bishamonten","Bishamonten","the Vaiśravaṇa of the north made the war god with the pagoda and the spear, the Kurama temple, Uesugi Kenshin's banner, the Seven Lucky Gods, the Tamonten of the Four Heavenly Kings"),
 ("japanese","konohanasakuya_hime","Konohanasakuya-hime","the blossom princess wife of Ninigi who bore in the burning hut to prove her fidelity, the goddess of Mount Fuji (the Sengen shrines), the sake and the cherry blossom, the sister Iwanaga-hime refused (the mortality of emperors)"),
 ("japanese","toyotama_hime","Toyotama-hime","the sea king's daughter who married Hoori and gave birth as a crocodile (or dragon) and was seen, the grandmother of Jimmu, the Melusine motif, the Kagoshima shrines"),
 ("japanese","tenjin","Tenjin (Sugawara no Michizane)","the exiled scholar (d. 903) whose angry ghost struck the palace with lightning and was appeased as Tenman Tenjin, the god of learning, the Kitano and Dazaifu shrines, the students' plaques, the goryō cult as a type"),
